  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Store attributes internally in a Map<String, String[]>, thus removing a whole lot of conditional logic and behavioral inconsistency.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Create separate methods for set(String, String) and set(String, String[]) instead of accepting either in set(String, Object).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Modify getString(String) so it will return the single value (if any) that was stored under that key. If strict upward compatibility is required, it could throw a ClassCastException if more than one value is stored. More likely, it would be acceptable to either return the first such value, or to throw an IllegalStateException.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Modify method signatures to throw specific exceptions (NullPointerException, IllegalArgumentException, etc.) instead of bare Exception.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Genericize method signatures and internal variables.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
